<title>USA: Paxson Q4 oper cash flow rises to $13.2 mln.</title>
<headline>Paxson Q4 oper cash flow rises to $13.2 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WEST PALM BEACH, Fla. 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the three months ended December 31</p>
<p>				    1996			 1995</p>
<p> Oper cash flow(a)    $    13,170		$     8,740</p>
<p> Revs			    55,513		     31,550</p>
<p>				For the 12 months ended December 31</p>
<p> Oper cash  flow(a)	  43,574		     24,299</p>
<p> Revs			   165,014		    103,074</p>
<p>(All data above 000s)</p>
<p>(a) Net income excluding non-cash items, non-recurring items  including terminated operations, interest, other income, income taxes and time brokerage fees, less scheduled program rights payments.  Segment Operating Cash Flow is computed prior to corporate allocation.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
